  "instruction": "I need to discover exactly what preconditions this repair-desk app enforces before a ticket can be marked Ready. Use a throwaway scratch ticket to probe this: create a new ticket titled 'fwrd72-n1 RD Scratch Probe' (customer 'Probe'), then click Mark Ready on it with NO parts and read the exact refusal/error message the app shows (it may list unmet requirements). Then, step by step, add/adjust the minimum needed (e.g. add a part, fill fields) retrying Mark Ready after each change until it is accepted, noting exactly which change made it pass. You may also inspect the app's client code (app.js) for the Ready-precondition rules to confirm. When done, remove the scratch ticket completely (delete it if the app allows, otherwise archive it) so nothing from the probe is left active. Report: the exact refusal message text, the exact list of unmet requirements it named, and exactly which change(s) were required to make Mark Ready succeed.",
